commit 4561ebd9d73b32b39b9c558e7507a3827270fb76
Author: Stephen P. Hurlsmith <sphurlsmith@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 24 13:44:54 2025 +0300

    Restructured makefile system, directory tree, and added program options features
    
    What it says on the title is what you get!  I decided to do some research
    over how makefiles should work, and used a recursive makefile system
    for getting my files up to date, as well as actually using make correctly
    to shorten compile times.  Now when you run make it doesn't update every
    single file!  It goes into directories, like a big-boy project
    
    And to assist the big-boy ideas, I decided I'd also start writing better
    C++ code.  Reading computer science books helped out, and scouring the
    c++ documentation was similarly helpful.  I use templates now!
    
    And of course the biggest change is something very clear: the directory
    structure has been revised. Now we have src and include for src and
    include files, instead of mixing them. Outside libraries have been
    kept in their own sub-source-directory called lib, and have a subdirectory
    include/lib
    
    I also removed the docs directory since I'd like to write documentation
    separately.  I'm not sure about running a MediaWiki server on my laptop,
    and I'm similarly not privy to writing literal org-mode document trees
    for Wawacraft:Evolved.  I think I'd have to make a series of HTML files
    for all documentation, since I'm used to it.  I'll use org mode to export
    the files, and a custom CSS skin will make it all the better.
    
    In other news, we still don't have an organization for testing, so stuff
    still goes into main.cpp temporarily.
    
    But hey, a big update starting a revision like this always starts slow,
    and with my previous knowledge, I'll have made the BEST technical successor
    to Wawacraft!
    
    PS: Sneek peek option --otm gives you an ominous, haunting message!
    
    WAWACRAFT:EVOLVED FOREVER!!

