commit b81e9564a4cf0446c0ffb3f05cde984f2b2183a9
Author: Stephen P. Hurlsmith <sphurlsmith@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Apr 21 13:57:40 2025 +0300

    Fixed voxel raycasting system
    
    This commit and the previous has fixed the issues of block placement and
    deletion. The raycasting algorithm has been fixed to be used comfortably,
    and the block placement and deletion algorithms have been configured to
    work across chunks and in the current chunk well.
    
    Nice commit, though I don't have time to improve other things. I have thought
    of a relay system for controls that buffers key state every frame, and
    determines when a key press can be registered based on its previous state.
    If the previous frame was pressed, this frame is ignored. Otherwise, the
    key press is registered. I'm pretty sure this is the way that most games work,
    and this solution doesn't rely on setting limits of operation per frame.
    I did benefit from setting a limit though, at least to make sure that block
    presses aren't a problem.
    
    Will look further into code standards, documentation, etc.

