commit 5fe3b970564421b75246d58583c21468a62a0344
Author: Stephen P. Hurlsmith <sphurlsmith@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Feb 19 18:28:50 2025 +0300

    Fixed the bug and realized my thing is like super fast
    
    It wasn't an issue of rounding error, in fact it turns out I have
    a very intelligent design for it. The error was that I was unloading
    chunks AFTER I created the visible list(which holds references to
    indexes in the chunk array), which invalidated the visibility list in
    some cases. Now terrain works completely with all kinds of coordinates,
    as I unload unneeded chunks BEFORE I find the visible chunks and
    set their references for the frame.

