commit 1cefd1efab459c1fc142443a1ac1435443f8784f
Author: Stephen P. Hurlsmith <sphurlsmith@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jan 21 18:17:53 2025 +0300

    Changes to the structure of render_environment and its render callback
    
    As it is already known, render_environment is a render environment
    holding a pointer to both types of meshes, which casts these types
    to void pointers to get them to pass through to the class window, which
    later sends it to a user-defined callback which can cast these back
    in a canonical use of the engine to a mesh_3d or whatever they may so
    like :).
    
    Now these pointers have been updated to mesh_base** and mesh_3d** to allow
    for more meshes to be given, preferrably through a mesh*[] which holds pointers
    to all the meshes you need to render.
    
    I've seen relatively good success in fixing this issue on the rewrite,
    and will try to see what I can do to try and make textures work
    such that multiple textures can render at once. Currently, there is a
    bug where only the first binded texture works. Perhaps you need to bind
    the textures manually first? Though I do do that already...
    
    Well, that's a good commit for the day, isn't it?
    
    WAWACRAFT:EVOLVED FOREVER!!!

