commit aeab931bf7e0abf5700afeb3cfddf15bac6d5c82
Author: sphurlsmith <sphurlsmith@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 31 10:13:36 2024 +0300

    October 31st Commit!
    
    We could call this Alpha 0.0.1, though I have not uploaded any of this work
    to the repo quite yet. Fixed up the quaternion rotation, and now we can use
    the arrow keys to rotate the camera in place to view around the cube.
    
    We have a couple of bugs - however - which require some attention in further
    commits:
            - Orientation can be flipped if you make a diagonal view shift
            - View matrix makes it so that the wawa cube rotates around the
              origin rather than the camera place. This ties into the fact that
            - The movement is completely separate from the rotation!!! The
              target vector isnt handled well, as it is quite literally never
              altered throughout the program run. I left it so because I was
              preventing another bug where the target vector would update constantly,
              making a dizzying effect of the camera being in constant rotation.
            - Sometimes, the program boots with multiples of e in the view matrix,
              corrupting the projection. As a result, you can get 'cursed boots' of
              Wawacraft Alpha 0.0.1, where the wawa cube is non existent (or rather
              just in a very far place outside of render distance).
    
    Regardless, we have made considerable progress. I almost went crazy trying to
    see where the bugs were in my quaternion class implementation were. Turns out
    I never really checked for the static quat quat::product() function.
    
    Wawacraft day is 19th of January. Wawacraft:Evolved day is 31st of October. A
    much better day than Halloween.
    
    PS: If you dont see an Alpha 0.0.1 (or 0.0.0 since thats more fitting) tag,
    then remember that I suck at using git. No problem though.
    
    Its been a crazy few weeks.
    
    Wawacraft Evolved Forever!!!

