commit e7de903025615fe274c5a3f2a2411163f655e500
Author: sphurlsmith <sphurlsmith@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 15 11:40:14 2024 +0300

    Corrected Texture Mapping!!
    
    Turns out, you don't need to do any fancy math, because GLSL manages
    texture mapping for you. I was doing a manual perspective divide in the
    vertex shader. Once it is removed however, we immediately gain correct
    texture mapping thanks to OpenGL.
    
    This means that we no longer need the new shaders, just to correct the
    default shaders for texture mapping!

